# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed (this workspace produces binaries).

# --- Game data: NEVER commit ---
# Both data folders (docs/METHOD.md, "The data folder is read-only runtime input"): `TFD_DATA`,
# The First Descendant, which supplies the game's own meshes, textures and animation, and
# `MW2_DATA`, Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2 (2009), which supplies the sound effects. Each is
# read-only runtime input, resolved through the environment variable of its name; their contents,
# and any code derived from them, live outside this repository by rule. `/TFD_DATA` and
# `/MW2_DATA` are the dev links beside the checkout (symlinks to the real installs, or in-tree
# copies) — machine-local like the links, never committed; `scripts/data-guard.sh` fails the gates
# when anything under a resolved folder is tracked.
/TFD_DATA
/TFD_DATA/
/MW2_DATA
/MW2_DATA/

# Real data files used as test fixtures (document expected paths, do not commit).
**/tests/fixtures/

# --- the one folder the game persists into ---
# config, saves, settings. Machine-local by definition: `crates/spdesc`'s local-state module is
# the only thing in the tree that may write it.
/spdesc-config/

# Profiling output: `--features bevy/trace_chrome` drops a multi-GB flame chart in the cwd, which
# otherwise leaves the checkout "dirty".
trace-*.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
/.idea/
# Claude Code: settings and skills under .claude/ are each person's own.
/.claude/

# Python bytecode from the `scripts/` tooling.
__pycache__/

TASKBOARD.md
/*.log
